      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>datacenters</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array (string)</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The vCenter Datacenters in which the RHCOS vm guests are located. This field will be used by the Cloud Controller Manager. Each datacenter listed here should be used within a topology.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>port</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>integer</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>port is the TCP port that will be used to communicate to the vCenter endpoint. When omitted, this means the user has no opinion and it is up to the platform to choose a sensible default, which is subject to change over time.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
